      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that you are a mistake is a heavy, untrue narrative you've allowed to take root. True respect for your parents isn't found in erasing who you are, but in being honest about your own worth, even when it's messy. You don't need to be a perfect reflection of their past to honor them; your existence is already a part of their legacy in a way they might not even realize.",
      "source": "target",
